.TH rtd 1 "September 2024" "rtd 1.0" "Remote Terminal Daemon"
.SH NAME
rtd \- Remote terminal daemon for secure machine access

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rtd
.B \-p
.IR PASSWORD
.RB [\-l
.IR DIRECTORY ]
.RB [\-s
.IR SOCKET ]
.RB [\-h]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rtd
is a secure daemon that enables remote access to your machine via:
.IP \(bu 2
SSH through a Cloudflare tunnel
.IP \(bu 2
Browser-based web terminal
.IP \(bu 2
Agent-based command execution for tools like Claude Code

The daemon manages authentication, session isolation, hibernation states, and
optional filesystem sandboxing.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-p \fIPASSWORD\fR
.B Required.
Set the authentication password for all connections. The password is stored as
a secure hash using bcrypt algorithm with exponential backoff on failed attempts.
.TP
.B \-l \fIDIRECTORY\fR
Enable sandbox mode. When specified, all shell sessions are restricted to this
directory via chroot. Useful for running untrusted code or Claude Code in an
isolated environment.
.TP
.B \-s \fISOCKET\fR
Specify the Unix socket path for client connections
.RB (default:
.IR /tmp/rt.sock ).
.TP
.B \-h
Display help message and exit.

.SH FEATURES
.TP
.B Authentication
Password-based authentication with:
.IP \(bu 2
Bcrypt secure hashing
.IP \(bu 2
Failed attempt tracking (5 attempts max by default)
.IP \(bu 2
Exponential backoff lockout (30 seconds by default)
.TP
.B Session Management
.IP \(bu 2
Each connection runs in a separate process
.IP \(bu 2
PTY allocation for interactive shells
.IP \(bu 2
Session-specific working directory management
.IP \(bu 2
UUID-based session identification
.TP
.B Hibernation
.IP \(bu 2
Pause all remote access and close sessions
.IP \(bu 2
Useful when closing the laptop or locking the screen
.IP \(bu 2
Can be triggered via web control panel
.TP
.B Sandboxing
.IP \(bu 2
Optional chroot-based filesystem isolation
.IP \(bu 2
Restricts access outside the specified directory
.IP \(bu 2
Allows machine tools to function within sandbox

.SH USAGE EXAMPLES
.TP
Start the daemon with password protection:
.B rtd \-p "my_secure_password"

.TP
Start daemon with sandbox to a project directory:
.B rtd \-p "password" \-l /home/user/myproject

.TP
Use custom socket location:
.B rtd \-p "password" \-s /tmp/rt\-custom.sock

.SH SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS
.TP
.B Password Security
The password is stored as a bcrypt hash. It cannot be recovered from storage.
Use a strong, unique password.
.TP
.B Failed Attempts
After 5 failed authentication attempts, the daemon locks out for 30 seconds.
Subsequent attempts during lockout are rejected immediately.
.TP
.B Isolation
Each SSH connection runs in its own process with separate resources. Use
.B \-l
for additional filesystem isolation.
.TP
.B Transport Security
This daemon requires external encryption (Cloudflare tunnel or SSH protocol)
for protection during transit. Do not expose the socket directly to untrusted
networks.
.TP
.B Hibernation
Use hibernation mode when:
.IP \(bu 2
Laptop is closed
.IP \(bu 2
Screen is locked
.IP \(bu 2
You want to pause all remote access

.SH COMMANDS
.B rtd
communicates via the Unix socket with protocol commands:
.TP
.B AUTH:\fRPASSWORD
Authenticate with the daemon. Required before other commands.
.TP
.B SHELL:\fRDIRECTORY
Create a new shell session in the specified directory.
.TP
.B CD:\fRSESSION_ID:PATH
Change working directory for a session (if sandbox allows).
.TP
.B HIBERNATE
Enter hibernation mode (close all sessions, refuse new requests).
.TP
.B WAKE
Exit hibernation mode (resume accepting requests).

.SH ENVIRONMENT
The spawned shell inherits:
.IP \(bu 2
Current environment variables
.IP \(bu 2
User's shell from
.B SHELL
environment variable (defaults to /bin/bash)
.IP \(bu 2
Working directory specified at session creation

.SH FILES
.TP
.I /tmp/rt.sock
Default Unix socket for client connections. Can be changed with
.B \-s
option.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rt (1),
.BR chroot (2),
.BR ssh (1),
.BR openpty (3)

.SH AUTHOR
Implemented as part of the PUtils remote access suite.
